  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Usage of Socio-Economic Statistics for Economic Policy-Making IDF Grant</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This IDF grant proposal addresses the critical data area of National Accounts (NA).  Under-coverage, under-reporting, poor price statistics, etc. affect the quality of GDP estimates, both at current and constant prices, at quarterly level, and by final consumption/expenditure categories. As an initial step, the grant funds, will assist the SDS to strengthen the capacity of the NA Division to improve the methodology and techniques of the NA estimates and expand its data sources and improve the overall information basis of NA.  The IDF-financed activities are envisaged to support the set up and implementation of a new system of statistical survey necessary to improve and expand the NA data sources. TF056205 The purpose of the Grant is to assist the Recipient in strengthening the capacity of the Department of Statistics (DS) and improve the methodology and techniques in the System of National Accounts (SNA).</narrative>
  </description>
